Legacy QModem pages: tabs without links, and legend-headed cards

Pages that build their own markup in script, rather than through LuCI's forms, use two
patterns this theme did not cover. QModem's Advance Modem Settings is where both show:

- Its function tabs (Dial Mode, Rat Prefer, Set IMEI, ...) are bare <li> items with the text
  in them and no <a>. The tab rules style "li > a", so these got no padding, no rounding and
  no selected state: a run of cramped words with no sign of the open tab.
- Its cards are <fieldset class="cbi-section"> headed by a <legend>. A legend is drawn on the
  fieldset's border, so the card's header bar sat half outside the top of the card, cut
  through by the border line. QModem Information and SMS build theirs the same way.

The bare items now get the tab segment on the item itself, with the selected state. The
legend is floated, which makes it an ordinary box inside the card; it then takes the same
header bar as an h3, and what follows starts below it. Only top-level cards: a nested
section has no card padding for the bar to bleed into.

Both selectors match only these patterns: LuCI's own tabs keep their <a>, and its forms head
cards with h3, so no stock page changes.

Applies to: https://github.com/anothaDev/luci-theme-vantage.git @ v1.2.0 (a7ff63b7), after 0001.
Upstream status: local to CleanWRT.

--- a/luci-theme-vantage/htdocs/luci-static/vantage/vantage.css
+++ b/luci-theme-vantage/htdocs/luci-static/vantage/vantage.css
@@ -969,6 +969,15 @@
 	font-size: var(--fs-md); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.005em;
 }
 .cbi-section > .cbi-title > h3 { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-2); flex: 1 1 auto; margin: 0; font-size: var(--fs-md); font-weight: 600; }
+/* A <legend> heading a fieldset card (pages that build their cards in script, such as
+   QModem's) is drawn by the browser on the fieldset's border, so the header bar above sat
+   half outside the card. Floated, it is an ordinary box inside the card and takes the bar's
+   bleed like an h3; what follows starts below it. Top-level cards only: a nested section
+   has no card padding to bleed into. (CleanWRT: patches/packages/luci-theme-vantage/) */
+fieldset.cbi-section:not(.cbi-section *) > legend:first-child {
+	float: left; box-sizing: border-box; width: calc(100% + 2 * var(--card-px));
+}
+fieldset.cbi-section:not(.cbi-section *) > legend:first-child + * { clear: both; }
 /* headings further down a card: sub-section title with a hairline above */
 .cbi-section > h3:not(:first-child), .cbi-section > div > h3, .cbi-value > h4, .cbi-section-node > h4 {
 	display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-2);
@@ -1948,6 +1957,20 @@
 /* the selected segment carries the signal (text and ring): white on the
    grey track alone was hard to pick out; hover keeps it */
 .cbi-tabmenu > li.cbi-tab > a, .cbi-tabmenu > li.cbi-tab > a:hover, .vt-pagetabs > .vt-tab[aria-current] { background-color: var(--seg-on); color: var(--accent-text); font-weight: 600; box-shadow: var(--seg-on-ring); }
+/* tabs built as bare list items with no link inside (QModem's Advance Modem Settings):
+   the same segment, on the item itself (CleanWRT: patches/packages/luci-theme-vantage/) */
+.cbi-tabmenu > li:not(:has(> a)) {
+	align-items: center;
+	min-height: var(--ctl-h); padding: 0 10px;
+	border: 3px solid transparent; background-clip: padding-box;
+	border-radius: calc(var(--r) + 3px);
+	color: var(--text-2);
+	font-weight: 500;
+	white-space: nowrap;
+	cursor: pointer;
+}
+.cbi-tabmenu > li:not(:has(> a)):hover { color: var(--text); }
+.cbi-tabmenu > li.cbi-tab:not(:has(> a)) { background-color: var(--seg-on); color: var(--accent-text); font-weight: 600; box-shadow: var(--seg-on-ring); }
 .cbi-tabmenu > li[data-errors] > a::after {
 	content: attr(data-errors);
 	display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
